{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_06d78fafc485e15b09969c0f1ddd00baa1c543a6b4a22a9928b6b930ef473857"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Keyboard controls include Enter to submit, Ctrl+J for newline, empty Enter to rerun or explain output, Ctrl+R to rerun the last suggestion, Ctrl+S to copy, and !<cmd> to run shell commands directly."},{"claim_ids":["clm_087046fd7bb0daa0f796c75b7cc17188e7b757f677a6927a8fe4add502d332f2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Data is stored under ~/.ducky/ in files for prompt history, a JSON conversation log, user preferences including last model, and saved crumbs (crumbs.json)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0a8ae43598eac69ec4f997567eab67660fa4328fe24ad096bed18e6d65393e13"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Crumbs are saved command shortcuts supporting ${VAR} and $var placeholder styles, invoked by name with positional arguments that substitute into the stored command."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0f6dd66f7537ff7f924fbc69b45973a4855cf42db441883889f29400015a88c4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"CLI flags include --directory/-d to preload code, --model/-m, --local/-l (qwen3 default), and --yolo/-y to auto-run commands without confirmation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1cd9510270100dcc2dedfa54d80739f28ec2160a0bb65deaf9dc2704a1031522"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requirements are Ollama (local or cloud) and Python 3.10+; the requirements.txt lists 'ollama'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3df3886481fe64f9878b5ef505ad508c5a51754de4024dcd9c0ae58b8b30ff65"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo, run 'uv sync', run via 'uv run ducky', and lint with 'uv run ruff check .'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3f76fe42a1c917d31c20a69a7b7727bb2d78b9aea9814cc0b01a22cebd9ebcd6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is built around Ollama, supporting both local models (localhost:11434) and cloud models (ollama.com), with the last used model saved automatically."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5dbd97c4b02e028e4ff70c324ef61ef5039dfd7a4fb4142eb4bc908d7325b7d0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Both 'ducky' and 'rubber-ducky' executables work identically; global install via 'uv tool install rubber-ducky' is recommended, and uvx usage requires a '--' separator."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7f6a331eee4623bfec49b52f8dc55ca34479a37432efede0bc7530139617b7c0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers an interactive REPL launched with 'ducky' and a single-shot mode where a positional prompt yields one command suggestion that is copied to the clipboard."},{"claim_ids":["clm_886deaa6b53c3b442ee5e9d446e3695a4fd1ace4f3e1d66f19124f59239c37d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Piped input is supported, e.g. 'cat error.log | ducky \"what's wrong here?\"' or piping git diff for summarization."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a09c321a14672285262a98713673d0cad73040553bf2d253502d67c45d2ee233"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The --yolo flag appears to bypass the default confirmation step before executing suggested shell commands, implying execution normally requires user confirmation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e5a318fd102bf19bd852ae1d0d00303f05093a5373842aebfa2a5809183842d4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The REPL supports inline commands such as /help, /clear, /reset, /model, /local, /cloud, /run, /expand, plus crumb commands like /crumbs and /crumb add/del."}],"claim_ids":["clm_06d78fafc485e15b09969c0f1ddd00baa1c543a6b4a22a9928b6b930ef473857","clm_087046fd7bb0daa0f796c75b7cc17188e7b757f677a6927a8fe4add502d332f2","clm_0a8ae43598eac69ec4f997567eab67660fa4328fe24ad096bed18e6d65393e13","clm_0f6dd66f7537ff7f924fbc69b45973a4855cf42db441883889f29400015a88c4","clm_1cd9510270100dcc2dedfa54d80739f28ec2160a0bb65deaf9dc2704a1031522","clm_3df3886481fe64f9878b5ef505ad508c5a51754de4024dcd9c0ae58b8b30ff65","clm_3f76fe42a1c917d31c20a69a7b7727bb2d78b9aea9814cc0b01a22cebd9ebcd6","clm_5dbd97c4b02e028e4ff70c324ef61ef5039dfd7a4fb4142eb4bc908d7325b7d0","clm_7f6a331eee4623bfec49b52f8dc55ca34479a37432efede0bc7530139617b7c0","clm_886deaa6b53c3b442ee5e9d4